  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef and his family is trying to reach the airport. Including Chef, they are a total of NNN members.\n\nA single cab ride costs max⁡(200,100⋅X)\\max(200, 100 \\cdot X)max(200,100⋅X) rupees to transport XXX people from Chef's home to the airport. Further, a cab can fit **at most 4 people**.\n\nChef may have to book multiple cabs in order for his entire family to reach the airport. What is the minimum cost for Chef's family to reach the airport if they take cabs optimally?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the number of people in Chef's family.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum cost.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤501 \\le T \\le 501≤T≤50",
      "1≤N≤501 \\le N \\le 501≤N≤50"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1\n4\n5\n6",
        "output": "200\n400\n500\n600",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : Chef takes a cab alone, which costs him 200200200.\nTest Case 2 : All 444 members can fit in a single cab, costing max⁡(200,100⋅4)=400\\max(200, 100 \\cdot 4) = 400max(200,100⋅4)=400.\nTest Case 3 : 333 members take a single cab costing 300300300, and then the last 222 members take another cab costing 200200200."
      }
    ]
  },
